{% extends "legal.html.j2" %}
{% set updated = "2026-10-26" %}
{% block title %}Privacy{% endblock %}
{% block description %}{{ plugin.displayName }} collects no personal data: no telemetry, no accounts, no analytics. What runs where, and the third parties involved.{% endblock %}
{% block body %}
    <h1>Privacy</h1>
    <p class="lede">{{ plugin.displayName }} collects no personal data. The pack has no
      telemetry, no accounts and no analytics, and neither does this site.</p>

    <h2>What the pack is</h2>
    <p>Skills and rules are text files your coding agent reads on your machine. Snippets,
      templates and examples are Python you run in your own Blender. None of them send
      anything to us.</p>
    <p>One snippet, <code>snippets/extension-user-data.py</code>, shows how an add-on
      <em>you</em> write can fetch a URL. It only runs when Blender's
      <strong>Allow Online Access</strong> preference is on, and only if you copy it into
      your add-on and call it.</p>

    <h2>The optional live-session plugin</h2>
    <p><code>blender-live-session</code> is a separate, opt-in plugin. It launches the
      official Blender Lab MCP server with <code>uvx</code>, which downloads the server
      from projects.blender.org and its dependencies from PyPI. The server talks to
      Blender over <code>localhost</code> on your machine. Nothing goes to us.</p>

    <h2>Your AI agent</h2>
    <p>When your agent uses a skill, the skill text and anything the agent reads from your
      project go to your agent's model provider (for example Anthropic, OpenAI or Cursor)
      under that provider's privacy policy, not this one.</p>

    <h2>Hosting</h2>
    <p>The source lives on GitHub, and this site is served by GitHub Pages. GitHub may log
      technical data such as IP addresses when you visit or clone; see the
      <a href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement">GitHub General Privacy Statement</a>.
      The site sets no cookies and loads no third-party scripts or fonts.</p>
    <p>If you open an issue, discussion or pull request, what you post is public on GitHub.</p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>Questions go to
      <a href="{{ repo }}/discussions">GitHub Discussions</a>. For security problems, see
      <a href="{{ repo }}/blob/main/SECURITY.md">SECURITY.md</a>. Changes to this page are
      tracked in the repository's history. See also the <a href="../terms/">terms</a>.</p>
{% endblock %}
